      "created_at": "2013-04-17T07:50:31.000Z",
      "cooked": "<p>So now that the kickstarter is alive and out there, I finally have a better idea of how Galactic Strike Force works gameplay wise and what it's all about.</p>\n<p>However, I was wondering about the Aftermath phase.&nbsp; Is it really only restricted to the enemies and them replenshing their supplies? If so why not refer to it as the end phase? or even the Enemy Phase.&nbsp; I state this because looking at the five phases you have</p>\n<p><strong>T</strong>ravel<br><strong>R</strong>equition<br><strong>I</strong>nstall<br><strong>B</strong>attle<br><strong>A</strong>ftermath<br><br>Which spells out…TRIBA!..err…um…yeah.&nbsp; However if it were called the End Phase or Enemy Phase…It would than spell out TRIBE which in a way would be neat way to remember the order of the phases. Sort of how Dominion has it's ABC (Action, Buy, Cleanup) method of gameplay.<br><br>Corny I know…but I think that's what I'll be calling it - and it's little things like this that help me remember how a game is played.<br><br>Regardless…Great job Greater than Games,&nbsp; I can't wait to see what the next few days/weeks updates will reveal and hopefully have it in my hands in October. <img src=\"//forums.greaterthangames.com/images/emoji/apple/+1.png?v=9\" title=\":+1:\" class=\"emoji\" alt=\":+1:\">   <img src=\"//forums.greaterthangames.com/images/emoji/apple/+1.png?v=9\" title=\":+1:\" class=\"emoji\" alt=\":+1:\"></p>",
