      "raw": "So now that the kickstarter is alive and out there, I finally have a better idea of how Galactic Strike Force works gameplay wise and what it&#39;s all about.\n\nHowever, I was wondering about the Aftermath phase.&nbsp; Is it really only restricted to the enemies and them replenshing their supplies? If so why not refer to it as the end phase? or even the Enemy Phase.&nbsp; I state this because looking at the five phases you have\n\n<strong>T</strong>ravel<br /><strong>R</strong>equition<br /><strong>I</strong>nstall<br /><strong>B</strong>attle<br /><strong>A</strong>ftermath<br /><br />Which spells out...TRIBA!...err...um..yeah.&nbsp; However if it were called the End Phase or Enemy Phase...It would than spell out TRIBE which in a way would be neat way to remember the order of the phases. Sort of how Dominion has it&#39;s ABC (Action, Buy, Cleanup) method of gameplay.<br /><br />Corny I know...but I think that&#39;s what I&#39;ll be calling it - and it&#39;s little things like this that help me remember how a game is played.<br /><br />Regardless...Great job Greater than Games,&nbsp; I can&#39;t wait to see what the next few days/weeks updates will reveal and hopefully have it in my hands in October. :+1:   :+1: ",
